  "notes": [
    "`T` read in milliseconds, from the step and the coast: the median step between rows is 50, and the reader reads one above 5 as milliseconds (at the manuals' 1 to 33 samples a second, a step is 0.03 to 1 in seconds and 30 to 1,000 in milliseconds); on that clock `Alt` slows at 0.995 g in feet over the rows from 2.5 s to 5.5 s, up to the row before the marker `Apogee` at 6 s, where the reader takes 0.7 to 1.3 g in feet or in meters and a clock 1,000 times off would put it 10⁶ times off",
    "`Alt` read in feet, from the manual and the coast: the Classic and TRS manuals (p37) state feet; the Quantum and Proton manuals give every height in feet and no Eggtimer manual offers meters; over the rows from 2.5 s to 5.5 s, up to the row before the marker `Apogee` at 6 s, it slows at 0.995 g in feet, within the 0.7 to 1.3 g the reader takes, where in meters it would be 3.263 g",
    "`Veloc` read in feet per second, from the manual: the Classic and TRS manuals (p37) give the velocity in ft/sec, and the Proton's (p45) as the change in `Alt` over the step; it is the change in `Alt` over the step, within 1 % or 1 ft/s, in 51 of 51 rows after the first, where the reader asks 90 %",
    "`Filt_Alt` read in feet, from the manual and the coast: it is the logger's filtered `Alt` (Quantum p38, Proton p45), in feet; over the rows from 2.5 s to 5.5 s, up to the row before the marker `Apogee` at 6 s, it slows at 0.995 g in feet, within the 0.7 to 1.3 g the reader takes",
    "`FVeloc` read in feet per second, from the manual: the Proton's manual (p46) gives it as the change in the filtered altitude over the step, and the Excel guide (p7) graphs the velocity in ft/sec; it is the change in `Filt_Alt` over the step, within 1 % or 1 ft/s, in 51 of 51 rows after the first, where the reader asks 90 %",
    "the marker columns, kept as written: `LDA`, `LowV`, `Apogee`, `N-O`, `Drogue` and `Main`; each is 0 but at the sample that marks its event, where the Quantum's and Proton's manuals (p38, p46) put the raw altitude, in feet",
    "`ASL Alt.` read in feet, from its unit mark: the flight summary writes 1150 ft; the launch site's elevation above sea level, as the logger measured it (TRS manual p36)",
    "`Apogee` read in feet, from its unit mark: the flight summary writes 480 ft; the logger's apogee above its zero, kept beside the table's altitudes (TRS manual p36)",
    "`T @` and `Time @` read in seconds, from the manual: the TRS manual's download writes the flight summary's times in `secs.` (p36), and its LDA at 0.700 secs. as \"700ms into the flight\" (p37)",
    "the flight summary's times are its table markers' to the millisecond, one event each, the marker's: `Apogee` at `Apogee`, `LDA` at `LDA`, `Unlock` at `LowV`, `N-O` at `N-O`, `Drogue Deploy` at `Drogue`, `Main Deploy` at `Main`",
    "the flight summary's times of no marker in the table, each an event of its own: `Max Velocity`",
    "the flight settings, as the file writes them: `Drogue <1=Normal,2=Backup,0=OFF>` 1; `Main Altitude <50-2000 by 50, 0=OFF>` 300; `Frequency (Ctrl-F to change)` 915; `ID Code` 3",
    "1 line of the flight settings holds no setting: the name its owner gave the flight computer (TRS manual p24), left out of the record as free text that may name a person",
    "the flight summary's other lines, as the file writes them: `Base Temp: 68.0 F`; `Beep Code: 0`; `Last Flight Phase: 8` (main deployed, TRS manual p37); `Flight Time: 12.000`; `Max Velocity: 160 ft/sec`; `Avg Accel @ Max Veloc: 160.00 ft/sec2`; `G: 4.97`; `LDA: 65 ft`; `Altitude @ Unlock: 380 ft`; `Altitude @ N-O: 460 ft`; `Altitude @ Drogue Deploy: 460 ft`; `Altitude @ Main Deploy: 300 ft`"
  ]
}
